Description: fast, lightweight Linux system information fetch tool written in Rust
 KKFetch is a lightweight CLI system information fetch tool
 written in Rust for Linux systems. It gathers system specifications
 and displays them alongside distribution ASCII art logos using direct
 /proc, /sys, and POSIX probing where possible.
 .
 Features include:
  * Direct kernel and virtual filesystem telemetry (/proc, /sys, libc)
  * Comprehensive metrics: CPU, GPU, Memory, Storage, Packages, Kernel, Desktop
  * Multi-distro ASCII art logos with ANSI 256-color support
  * Shell completions for Bash, Zsh, and Fish
